So now the function becomes [e^x(e^x - 1)] / [2 cos(3x/2) sin(x/2)]. Maybe I can rewrite this in terms of known limits as x approaches 0. Let's recall that as x approaches 0, e^x - 1 ~ x (since the limit of (e^x - 1)/x is 1), and sin(x/2) ~ x/2 (since sin θ ~ θ when θ approaches 0). Let's try to express the numerator and denominator using these approximations.

